{"signature": "{\"model\": \"eleven_multilingual_v2\", \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\", \"settings\": {\"similarity_boost\": 0.85, \"stability\": 0.5, \"style\": 0.0, \"use_speaker_boost\": true}, \"text\": \"In Physics, a system is an object or group of objects being considered. We can track energy entering or leaving a system and energy transferred between stores within it. Energy is conserved: it does not vanish when a machine slows down or an object stops moving. It is transferred into other stores, often the internal energy stores of the objects and their surroundings. A helpful method is to identify the system, name the initial energy store, explain the transfer pathway and state which store increases. If there are several transfers, follow them in order. Remember that energy is measured in joules. One kilojoule equals one thousand joules, and one megajoule equals one million joules. Convert quantities into consistent units before comparing them.\", \"voice\": \"28e9d9dcea90e5b4\"}", "duration": 47.882449, "words": [["In", 0.0], ["Physics,", 0.221], ["a", 1.068], ["system", 1.254], ["is", 1.776], ["an", 1.927], ["object", 2.067], ["or", 2.554], ["group", 2.775], ["of", 3.065], ["objects", 3.251], ["being", 3.831], ["considered.", 4.122], ["We", 4.992], ["can", 5.178], ["track", 5.364], ["energy", 5.759], ["entering", 6.246], ["or", 6.827], ["leaving", 7.059], ["a", 7.43], ["system", 7.523], ["and", 7.941], ["energy", 8.127], ["transferred", 8.591], ["between", 9.23], ["stores", 9.613], ["within", 10.066], ["it.", 10.414], ["Energy", 11.157], ["is", 11.668], ["conserved:", 11.831], ["it", 12.771], ["does", 12.957], ["not", 13.201], ["vanish", 13.444], ["when", 13.932], ["a", 14.153], ["machine", 14.234], ["slows", 14.675], ["down", 15.07], ["or", 15.5], ["an", 15.744], ["object", 15.906], ["stops", 16.312], ["moving.", 16.719], ["It", 17.415], ["is", 17.601], ["transferred", 17.752], ["into", 18.402], ["other", 18.716], ["stores,", 19.018], ["often", 19.621], ["th